What:           /sys/class/power_supply/oplus-fastchg/priority
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Linux Power Supply Mailing List <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
                Read or replace the protocol probe order. Values are lowercase
                protocol names separated by whitespace, listed from highest to
                lowest priority. For example: "pps ufcs vooc".

                The initial order comes from the device tree's oplus,protocols
                property. A write must contain each configured protocol exactly
                once. Unknown, unconfigured, missing or repeated protocols, an
                empty value or embedded NUL bytes are rejected with EINVAL; the
                previous order remains unchanged. Writes during initialization,
                protocol probing or removal return EBUSY.

                Updates are atomic and affect the next complete probe pass.
                Writing this attribute does not restart detection, switch an active
                charging session or change charger-type and safety checks.
                The setting lasts until the driver is reloaded or the device
                reboots, when the device-tree default is restored.
